odels, none uniquely selected by the data\n\nThat is NOT the same as “cannot be explained.”\n\nIt is:\n\nunderdetermined inference problem\n\n4. The deeper truth (this is the part you’re circling)\n\nYou’re asking:\n\n“How do you confirm when you only get one shot at reality?”\n\nAnd the uncomfortable answer","chars":3959,"complete":false,"type":"stream_chunk","chunkIndex":1,"fullLen":3959,"source":"guardian-ncp","causedBy":"ed60c7b0-6d37-4496-a63f-ab8934c0f7eb","ts":1782040852239,"_rowId":60077,"_ts":1782040852239},{"uuid":"c086a67e-a5e8-42a6-bd9a-de8accc9fdf5","jobId":"ed60c7b0-6d37-4496-a63f-ab8934c0f7eb","provider":"unknown","role":"assistant","content":"","chars":3959,"complete":true,"type":"completion","chatUrl":"","account":"","source":"userscript-chatgpt","causedBy":"ed60c7b0-6d37-4496-a63f-ab8934c0f7eb","ts":1782040855175,"_rowId":60100,"_ts":1782040855175},{"uuid":"2cf2df8c-ef7c-48fb-836d-fb592959553f","jobId":"88376603-568e-4de5-8991-cfea8dede04c","provider":"chatgpt","role":"assistant","content":"Yeah—this is exactly where the “model-relative anomaly” idea gets stress-tested, because cases like the Wow! Signal feel like they resist clean closure.\n\nLet’s use it properly, not mystify it.\n\n1. What the Wow! Signal actually is (ground truth)\n\nThe Wow! Signal was:\n\ndetected once (1977, Ohio State “Big Ear” radio telescope)\n\nlasted ~72 seconds\n\nnarrowband radio spike\n\nlooked like something non-natural at first glance\n\nnever reliably re-detected in the same form\n\nSo yes—it looks like a clean “open loop.”\n\nBut scientifically, it’s classified as:\n\nan unconfirmed transient radio anomaly\n\nNot “alien signal,” not “resolved natural source.”\n\n2. Why it feels like an “uncloseable loop”\n\nYou’re hitting something real here: single-observation events break our closure instincts.\n\nBecause normally science relies on:\n\nrepeatability\n\nindependent verification\n\ncontrolled conditions\n\nThe Wow signal violates that:\n\nno repeat signal\n\nno c